Hi,

yes, you might have to do it in chunks.  By default
readSequenceMatrix() returns a character matrix, but if you can work
with a raw matrix that will be more memory efficient, because
internally the data is read as such and then coerced to a character
matrix, and that is memory expensive.

Try

seq <- readSequenceMatrix(acs, what="raw");
str(seq);

You can then coerce that matrix to characters, to integers, ... in
chunks, if you need coercing.

/Henrik

